      "role": "user",
      "content": "I built a regulatory network for rice drought response last year and saved it as a weighted edge list: column one is the transcription factor, column two is the gene it targets, and column three is the edge score. TF and gene identifiers are separate. I'd like to find modules that group TFs together with the genes they control."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like to find modules that group TFs together with the genes they control.\" -- the request does not say whether one item may belong to several groups at once: if one group each: CONDOR; if several groups at once: no registered workflow gives this.\n\nBefore I choose a workflow, please tell me: Should each gene, regulator or sample belong to one group only (one group each), or may one belong to several groups at once?\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
